  "question": {
    "text": "Let $f: R \\rightarrow R$ be defined as $f(x)=\\frac{x^{2}-x+4}{x^{2}+x+4}$. Then, range of the function $f(x)$ is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "jujVN",
      "text": "$\\left[\\frac{3}{5}, \\frac{5}{3}\\right]$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "pgH6Z",
      "text": "$\\left(\\frac{3}{5}, \\frac{5}{3}\\right)$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "OFujL",
      "text": "$\\left(-\\infty, \\frac{3}{5}\\right) \\cup\\left(\\frac{5}{3}, \\infty\\right)$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "Nl0hl",
      "text": "$\\left[-\\frac{5}{3},-\\frac{3}{5}\\right]$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Let $y=\\frac{x^{2}-x+4}{x^{2}+x+4}$\r\n$\\Rightarrow \\quad x^{2} y+x y+4 y=x^{2}-x+4$\r\n$\\Rightarrow(y-1) x^{2}+(y+1) x+4 y-4=0$\r\nFor $x$ to be real, discriminant of the above quadratic equation should be greater than equal to 0 \r\n$\\\\ \\Rightarrow \\quad(y+1)^{2}-4(y-1)(4 y-4) \\geq 0$\r\n$\\Rightarrow \\quad(y+1)^{2}-16(y-1)^{2} \\geq$\r\n$\\Rightarrow(y+1+4 y-4)(y+1-4 y+4) \\geq$\r\n$(5 y-3)(5-3 y) \\geq 0$\r\n$\\therefore \\quad y \\in\\left[\\frac{3}{5}, \\frac{5}{3}\\right]$",
    "image": null
  },
